 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "menachot.44b.11",
   "daf": "44b",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: מִנַּיִן לְכׇל הַנִּיתָּנִין עַל מִזְבֵּחַ הַחִיצוֹן שֶׁנְּתָנָן בְּמַתָּנָה אַחַת שֶׁכִּיפֵּר? שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״וְדַם זְבָחֶיךָ יִשָּׁפֵךְ עַל מִזְבַּח ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ״.",
   "en": "Apropos this statement, «the Sages taught» in a baraita: «From where» is it derived with regard «to all» offerings «whose» blood is to be «placed on the external altar that» if «one placed their» blood «with one» act of «placement,» as opposed to the two or four that are required depending upon the offering, «that» the offering has nevertheless «effected atonement» after the fact, i.e., one has fulfilled his obligation to bring the offering? «As it is stated: “And the blood of your offerings shall be poured out against the altar of the Lord your God”» (Deuteronomy 12:27)."
  }
 ],
